Q: Can System.Text.Json tolerate an unrecognized type discriminator during deserialization? A: <p>AFAIK since you are using interface here there is no way to define the fallback type in <code>System.Text.Json</code> at the moment.</p>
<p>You have following options - use a concrete type as a base type for your hierarchy:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>[JsonPolymorphic(IgnoreUnrecognizedTypeDiscriminators = true)]
[JsonDerivedType(typeof(KnownBarViaConcrete), nameof(KnownBarViaConcrete))]
public class Bar { } // will fallback to it

public class KnownBarViaConcrete : Bar { }

class Foo
{
    public required string Hello { get; init; }
    public required Bar? Bar { get; init; } // use concrete type
}
</code></pre>
<p>Or write custom serializer which will process the discriminator &quot;manually&quot;. Something to give you an idea:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>class BarConverter : JsonConverter&lt;IBar&gt;
{
    public override IBar? Read(ref Utf8JsonReader reader, Type typeToConvert, JsonSerializerOptions options)
    {
        // Copy reader so we can advance the token stream separately.
        // not sure how safe it is but based on quick search it should do the trick
        var copy = reader;
        copy.Read();
        var discriminatorProperty = copy.GetString();
        copy.Read();
        var discriminatorValue = copy.GetString();
        var targetType = discriminatorValue switch
        {
            &quot;KnownBar&quot; =&gt; typeof(KnownBar),
            &quot;AnotherKnownBar&quot; =&gt; typeof(AnotherKnownBar),
            _ =&gt; typeof(KnownBar) // Fallback
        };


        return JsonSerializer.Deserialize(ref reader, targetType, options) as IBar;
    }

    public override void Write(Utf8JsonWriter writer, IBar value, JsonSerializerOptions options) =&gt; throw new NotImplementedException();
}
</code></pre>
<p>There is feature request for ability to provide a fallback type, but currently it is not known when it will be implemented - see the <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/111755" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Fallback to configurable type for JsonPolymorphic deserialization</a> issue @github</p>

Q: How to make a generic specifiable associated type in Swift? A: <p>From what I understand Swift doesn't support generic associated types. The syntax <code>associatedtype Storage&lt;X&gt;</code> is invalid: assoicated types cannot have their own generic parameters.</p>
<h2>Solutions</h2>
<p><strong>Option 1: Make the Storage the primary generic parameter</strong></p>
<p>Flip the relationship: parameterize by storage, derive size from it:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>protocol SizeSpecifier {
    static var size: Int { get }
}

enum Num1: SizeSpeifier { static let size = 1 }
enum Num2: SizeSpeifier { static let size = 2 }
enum Num3: SizeSpeifier { static let size = 3 }

protocol _Storage {
    associatedtype Element
    associatedtype Size: SizeSpecifier
    init(repeating: Element)
}

struct _Storage1&lt;E&gt;: _Storage {
    typealias Size = Num1; typealias Element = E
    var cells: (E)
    init(repeating e: E) { cells = e }
}

struct _Storage2&lt;E&gt;: _Storage {
    typealias Size = Num2; typealias Element = E
    var cells: (E, E)
    init(repeating e: E) { cells = (e, e) }
}

struct _Storage3&lt;E&gt;: _Storage {
    typealias Size = Num3; typealias Element = E
    var cells: (E, E, E)
    init(repeating e: E) { cells = (e, e, e) }
}

struct StackArray&lt;Storage: _Storage&gt; {
    typealias Size = Storage.Size
    typealias Element = Storage.Element
    var _storage: Storage
}

// Usage
var arr = StackArray(_storage: _Storage3(repeating: 42))
print(Storage.Size.size) // 3
</code></pre>
<p>Add typealiases for cleaner API:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>typealias StackArray1&lt;E&gt; = StackArray&lt;_Storage1&lt;E&gt;&gt;
// ...

let arr: StackArray3&lt;Int&gt; = ...
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Option 2: make <code>SizeSpecifier</code> generic (if acceptable)</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>protocol SizeSpecifier {
    associatedtype Element
    associatedtype Storage: _Storage where Storage.Element == Element
    static var size: Int { get }
}

struct Num1&lt;E&gt;: SizeSpecifier {
    typealias Element = E
    typealias Storage = _Storage&lt;E&gt;
    static var size: Int { 1 }
}

struct StackArray&lt;Size: SizeSpecifier&gt; {
    var _storage: Size.storage
}

// Usage: StackArray&lt;Num3&lt;Int&gt;&gt;
</code></pre>
